Writer: a paragraph's direct property values are looked up by walking its property map once.

getDirectPropertyValuesTolerant (and getPropertyValuesTolerant) on a paragraph receive their property names in
ascending order, as the XTolerantMultiPropertySet contract requires; the DOCX/RTF table style pass asks for all
~400 of them for every table cell paragraph. Each name was found with its own binary search over the paragraph
property map, about nine string compares per name: 3 % of the open of a 3000-page report with tables.
HstSortedPropertyLookup (new hstsortedpropertylookup.cxx) keeps its position in the sorted map and steps forward
to the next name; a name out of order, or far ahead, is found with SfxItemPropertyMap::getByName as before, so
the entries found are the same for any list of names.

